  "experiment": "two-update-predecessor-coherent-density-flux",
  "result": "The predecessor-coherent signed density, terminal flux, and bottom-correction language is infeasible with or without time parity, both at alpha=8 and for every variable alpha>=0.",
  "evidence": "The 128 shared seven-bit words give exactly 20 adjacent-row states and 44 coherent edges. Exact integer Farkas identities are 0>=2 (9 rows) without time parity and 0>=6 (24 rows) with it.",
